                blog19Meta: "October 17, 2026 · Zero · Initial Release · Portable Uninstaller & Task Manager",
                blog19Title: "Zero version 0.0.1",
                blog19Desc: "Announcing Zero v0.0.1! A modern, ultra-lightweight, cross-platform portable standalone uninstaller, deep residual cleaner, and real-time process manager built with C++17, native Win32, and Qt6 with zero bloat and 100% offline privacy.",
                blog19Author: "Hamza Bellouch",
                authorRole19: "CEO & Founder of tknoglobal",
                blog19Intro: "We are thrilled to announce the initial release of Zero (v0.0.1)! Zero is an ultra-fast, lightweight, and privacy-focused cross-platform utility engineered to give users uncompromising control over their software and system resources. It unites an application uninstaller, an intelligent deep residual cleaner, and an active real-time process manager into a single self-contained portable tool with zero installation and complete privacy.",
                blog19Subhead1: "Pure Portable Standalone Architecture & Sibling App Protection",
                blog19Body1: "Zero is built using modern C++17 with strict RAII and zero external runtime dependencies. On Windows, it operates as a single standalone Win32 binary compiled with a static C++ runtime (/MT), launching in under 100ms with a sub-10MB memory footprint. On Linux and macOS, Zero delivers native performance through a modern Qt6 interface. Its revolutionary Sibling Application Protection engine prevents accidental deletion of shared vendor components, while Recycle Bin integration ensures complete file recoverability.",
                blog19Subhead2: "Changes — October 17, 2026",
                blog19Feat1: "Initial release of Zero v0.0.1 establishing the core portable standalone foundation.",
                blog19Feat2: "Desktop application uninstaller for 32-bit and 64-bit software with deep registry enumeration.",
                blog19Feat3: "Windows Store (UWP / MSIX) app management and clean PowerShell uninstallation.",
                blog19Feat4: "Intelligent deep residual cleaner scanning AppData, ProgramData, and Software registry hives.",
                blog19Feat5: "Heuristic Sibling Application Protection preventing damage to shared vendor installations.",
                blog19Feat6: "Safe file deletion routed through the operating system Recycle Bin for full recovery.",
                blog19Feat7: "Real-time task manager tracking CPU %, RAM, disk I/O throughput, and network transfer rates.",
                blog19Feat8: "Automatic multi-instance process grouping and one-click process tree termination.",
                blog19Feat9: "Instant substring search with custom owner-drawn capsule controls and zero UI stutter.",
                blog19Feat10: "Modern dark theme with vivid coral accents and Per-Monitor High-DPI (v2) dynamic scaling.",
                blog19Feat11: "Cross-platform Qt6 architecture for seamless execution on Linux and macOS.",
                blog19Feat12: "100% offline operation with zero analytics, zero telemetry, and zero background services.",
                blog19Subhead3: "Downloads & Release Assets",
                blog19Body2: "Zero v0.0.1 is available now on GitHub Releases. Download the portable standalone binary for Windows, Linux, or macOS, and enjoy an uninstaller and task manager with zero bloat and total privacy.",
                feedbackTitle19: "Ready to test Zero v0.0.1?",
                feedbackDesc19: "Download the standalone portable release directly from our official GitHub repository.",
                blogDateOct16: "October 16, 2026",
                blog18Meta: "October 16, 2026 · Agent Skills · Major Release · Version 2.2.0",
                blog18Title: "Agent Skills v2.2.0",
                blog18Desc: "Announcing Agent Skills v2.2.0! Surpassing 850+ production skills with 84 new additions: the complete OpenAI Codex Security suite (15 audit skills), Math Library (28 skills + math-master router), Physics Library (41 skills + physics-master router), runnable Python simulation tools, and standardized metadata.",
                blog18Author: "Hamza Bellouch",
                authorRole18: "CEO & Founder of tknoglobal",
                blog18Intro: "We are thrilled to announce Agent Skills v2.2.0! This landmark expansion scales our open-source agentic library past 850 production-grade skills by introducing 84 new specialized capabilities. Highlights include the complete OpenAI Codex Security suite with automated vulnerability scanning, comprehensive Math and Physics libraries coordinated by intelligent master routers, and embedded Python calculation scripts for rigorous symbolic and numerical computing.",
                blog18Subhead1: "Scientific Modeling, Master Routers & Codex Security Audit",
                blog18Body1: "Version 2.2.0 integrates dedicated master routers (math-master and physics-master) that automatically orchestrate specialized domain skills across linear algebra, calculus, discrete math, classical mechanics, thermodynamics, electromagnetism, and quantum physics. Furthermore, the OpenAI Codex Security suite brings 15 rigorous static code analysis and taint tracking skills designed to proactively catch vulnerabilities in AI-generated software.",
                blog18Subhead2: "Changes — October 16, 2026",
                blog18Feat1: "Integrated the full OpenAI Codex Security suite containing 15 automated vulnerability scanning and audit skills.",
                blog18Feat2: "Added the complete Math Skills Library powered by the central math-master router and 28 domain skills.",
                blog18Feat3: "Incorporated the Physics Skills Library guided by the physics-master router and 41 specialized physics skills.",
                blog18Feat4: "Embedded runnable Python calculation tools and numerical simulation scripts for symbolic math and physics.",
                blog18Feat5: "Standardized metadata JSON index files for all 84 newly introduced skills.",
                blog18Feat6: "Refreshed the main project documentation and repository tree to reflect more than 850 production skills.",
                blog18Feat7: "Eliminated all naming collisions by grouping new libraries into dedicated modular categories.",
                blog18Feat8: "Committed and pushed all updates directly to the remote GitHub main branch.",
                blog18Subhead3: "Open-Source Repository & Ecosystem Integration",
                blog18Body2: "Agent Skills v2.2.0 is live now on our official GitHub repository. Integrate the expanded catalog into Claude Code, Gemini CLI, Cursor, and Codex workflows to supercharge autonomous engineering today.",
                feedbackTitle18: "Ready to explore Agent Skills v2.2.0?",
                feedbackDesc18: "Inspect the 850+ skill catalog or download the latest release tag directly on GitHub.",
                blog17Meta: "October 16, 2026 · Links · New version · Release notes",
                blog17Title: "Links version 0.0.6-beta",
                blog17Desc: "Announcing Links v0.0.6-beta! Featuring a brand-new logo, multi-format QR export (PNG, JPG, WebP, PDF), dedicated customization panels, full offline Noto Sans Arabic typography across all styles, and key Look & Feel dark theme fixes.",
                blog17Author: "Hamza Bellouch",
                authorRole17: "CEO & Founder of tknoglobal",
                blog17Intro: "We are thrilled to announce the release of Links v0.0.6-beta! This release brings a fresh new logo, powerful multi-format QR code exports supporting PNG, JPG, WebP, and printable PDFs, intuitive on-screen customization panels, deep offline integration of the Noto Sans Arabic font family across all weights, and essential visual polish throughout.",
                blog17Subhead1: "Multi-Format QR Export & Dedicated Customization Panels",
                blog17Body1: "Links v0.0.6-beta expands QR code sharing by introducing high-resolution exports for PNG, JPG, WebP, and multi-page printable PDF documents. Designers and power users can now customize colors and dot patterns seamlessly through dedicated interactive panels placed directly beneath the live QR preview, backed by unified capsule button dimensions and cleaner, borderless format selectors.",
