                blog16Meta: "October 16, 2026 · Apex · New version · Release notes",
                blog16Title: "Apex version 0.1.1-beta",
                blog16Desc: "Announcing Apex v0.1.1-beta! Dedicated Dark Theme page with pure AMOLED black support, overhauled App Details with circular quick action buttons, robust language switching architecture with dynamic JSON translations, 3-step onboarding, and essential system app protection.",
                blog16Author: "Hamza Bellouch",
                authorRole16: "CEO & Founder of tknoglobal",
                blog16Intro: "We are thrilled to announce the release of Apex v0.1.1-beta! This milestone update delivers a dedicated Dark Theme preference screen with pure AMOLED black backgrounds, overhauled App Details with four circular quick action buttons, a hardened multilingual switching architecture with dynamic JSON pack lookup, an interactive 3-step onboarding flow, and core system safeguards.",
                blog16Subhead1: "Dedicated Dark Theme Preferences & AMOLED Black Support",
                blog16Body1: "Apex v0.1.1-beta introduces a dedicated DarkThemePreferences screen with LargeTopAppBar collapsible scrolling. Users can choose between Follow System (with distinctive Android icon), Dark Mode, and Light Mode, each accompanied by descriptive subtitles. A high-contrast toggle delivers pure AMOLED black backgrounds for OLED displays, backed by a centralized DarkThemePreference data model in PreferenceUtil and an app-wide LocalDarkTheme CompositionLocal ensuring instant, zero-latency visual reactivity across every screen.",
                blog16Subhead2: "Changes — October 16, 2026",
                blog16Feat1: "Dedicated Dark Theme preferences page featuring a modern collapsible LargeTopAppBar",
                blog16Feat2: "Distinctive Android, Dark Mode, and Light Mode icons for each theme option",
                blog16Feat3: "Clear explanatory descriptions beneath every theme choice",
                blog16Feat4: "High contrast dark theme toggle delivering pure AMOLED black backgrounds for OLED screens",
                blog16Feat5: "New PreferenceSwitchVariant UI component styled for secondary toggle settings",
                blog16Feat6: "Upgraded PreferenceSingleChoiceItem component supporting leading icons and subtitles",
                blog16Feat7: "Centralized DarkThemePreference data model and reactive state flow in PreferenceUtil",
                blog16Feat8: "App-wide LocalDarkTheme CompositionLocal for instant theme reactivity across all screens",
                blog16Feat9: "Integrated pure black color overrides into ApexTheme when high contrast mode is active",
                blog16Feat10: "Fixed the extra top spacing above the back button to perfectly match other settings pages",
                blog16Feat11: "Removed the tinted container bar on scroll so the top app bar smoothly matches the background",
                blog16Feat12: "Complete English and Arabic localization for all newly added options and descriptions",
                blog16Feat13: "Added an Advanced section in General Settings with a History toggle to enable or disable activity logging",
                blog16Feat14: "Implemented automatic dimming and disabling of the History icon in Clean and Stop screens when History is turned off",
                blog16Feat15: "Protected essential system apps including Clock, Phone, Contacts, and active Keyboards from being force-stopped",
                blog16Feat16: "Replaced the bottom capsule button in App Details with four circular quick action buttons",
                blog16Feat17: "Fixed the Uninstall action with proper system permissions so apps can be uninstalled directly",
                blog16Feat18: "Added smart store detection to route the Update action to Google Play Store or Galaxy Store based on installation source",
                blog16Feat19: "Added a Launch action to open apps directly from their details view",
                blog16Feat20: "Added an App Info action that redirects users straight to the Android system settings for that app",
                blog16Feat21: "Integrated official Google Material Symbols Outlined vector icons for delete forever, code update, outward launch arrow, and info",
                blog16Feat22: "Accurate language switching ensuring tapping English, Arabic, French, or Follow System immediately activates the exact chosen language",
                blog16Feat23: "Reliable system locale detection querying the actual device configuration rather than altered internal values",
                blog16Feat24: "Seamless navigation retention keeping the language screen open during language changes without kicking you back to the home screen",
                blog16Feat25: "Stable list rendering with unique item keys to prevent touch target misalignment during right-to-left layout flips",
                blog16Feat26: "Full interactivity in the language download sheet allowing direct one-tap selection and activation of installed packs",
                blog16Feat27: "Working dynamic translations for downloaded JSON languages through proper resource entry name lookup",
                blog16Feat28: "Clean separation between built-in and downloaded languages to prevent the Android operating system from resetting custom packs",
                blog16Feat29: "Automatic text direction and BCP 47 tag sanitation ensuring custom languages render in their correct layout direction",
                blog16Feat30: "Updated Translate card description to state Help translate this app on GitHub repository",
                blog16Feat31: "Updated Translate card destination link directing users to the official GitHub language repository",
                blog16Feat32: "Interactive three-step onboarding flow guiding users through the core capabilities",
                blog16Feat33: "Crisp multi-color vector illustrations replacing low-resolution visual assets",
                blog16Feat34: "Dynamic Dark and Light theme adaptation for buttons and surface backgrounds",
                blog16Feat35: "Customized color scheme matching the Apex brand across all feature icons",
                blog16Feat36: "Accurate bilingual localizations in Arabic and English for all onboarding screens",
                blog16Feat37: "Modern Material 3 typography integration replacing legacy hardcoded font styling",
                blog16Feat38: "High-contrast pill buttons designed for smooth and accessible step navigation",
                blog16Feat39: "Aligned the Credits top bar layout and back navigation coordinates with the Troubleshooting page",
                blog16Feat40: "Enabled dynamic collapsing scroll animations for the Credits screen title",
                blog16Feat41: "Resolved the scrolling issue on the Credits page to allow smooth vertical scrolling",
