                blog10Meta: "July 18, 2026 · Agent Skills · Initial Release · Version 1.0.0",
                blog10Title: "Agent Skills v1.0.0",
                blog10Desc: "Initial release 1.0.0 establishing the project base for an extensible library of custom AI agent skills designed to automate complex development tasks, refactoring, and agentic workflows.",
                blog10Author: "Hamza Bellouch",
                authorRole10: "CEO & Founder of tknoglobal",
                blog10Intro: "We are excited to announce the initial release of Agent Skills (v1.0.0)! Establishing the project foundation for a modular, standardized library of custom AI agent skills designed to empower autonomous coding assistants with structured workflows and deep engineering expertise.",
                blog10Subhead1: "The Foundation for Agentic Engineering",
                blog10Body1: "Agent Skills v1.0.0 introduces a structured framework for defining, testing, and deploying specialized agent skills across diverse programming languages and development workflows. By pairing clear instructions with practical automation patterns, the suite enables AI agents to execute complex architectural refactorings, adherence checks, and multi-step tasks with high reliability and zero drift.",
                blog10Subhead2: "Changes — July 18, 2026",
                blog10Feat1: "Initial release 1.0.0 establishing the project base and core repository architecture.",
                blog10Feat2: "Created the project base with standardized skill specification guidelines and metadata schemas.",
                blog10Subhead3: "Open-Source Repository & Getting Started",
                blog10Body2: "The project is completely open source under our permissive licensing. You can explore the repository on GitHub, integrate skills into your own agent pipelines, or contribute new skill modules to help shape the future of autonomous software engineering.",
