                blog1Subhead1: "A Fresh, Modern UI Built for Speed and Control",
                blog1Body1: "Links is an open-source QR code and URL management suite for Android. In Version 0.0.4-beta, we completely revamped the scanning engine with multi-page PDF detection, intelligent Wi-Fi auto-classification, and dynamic target locking.",
                blog1Subhead2: "Key Highlights & Enhancements",
                blog1Feat1: "Scan and extract QR codes directly from multi-page PDF documents with automated detection.",
                blog1Feat2: "Smart Wi-Fi auto-classification with direct one-tap connection and password copying.",
                blog1Feat3: "Intelligent camera viewfinder with dynamic corner snapping and auto-alignment for tilted codes.",
                blog1Feat4: "Comprehensive history management with favorites, multi-format export (TXT, CSV, JSON, XLSX), and backup restore.",
                blog1Subhead3: "How to Test & Join the Beta",
                blog1Body2: "We are eager to hear your feedback on the v0.0.4-beta release! You can deploy and test it today from our GitHub repository. If you encounter any bugs or have feature suggestions, please join the discussion on our GitHub issues.",
                btnDownloadApk: "Download APK",
                allRightsReserved: "All Rights Reserved",
                privacyPolicy: "Privacy Policy",
                backToHome: "Back to Home",
                privBadge: "Official Policy & Security Terms",
                privTitle: "Privacy Policy",
                privLastUpdated: "Last Updated: October 2, 2026",
                privHeroIntro: "At Hamza Bellouch (tknoglobal), privacy is not an afterthought—it is the foundational core of everything we build. All our applications, software suites, tools, and projects operate under strict zero-tracking, zero-ad, and 100% on-device principles.",
                privRule0Title: "0. Rule 0: Disclaimer on Modified Builds, External Binaries & Unofficial Forks",
                privRule0Item1: "<strong>Original Source Integrity:</strong> This privacy policy, safety guarantees, and security features apply strictly and exclusively to official, unmodified application binaries, software packages, installers, scripts, extensions, and source code distributed directly through our official repositories (<a href=\"https://github.com/hamzabellouch\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-adguard underline font-semibold\">github.com/hamzabellouch</a>) and verified releases.",
                privRule0Item2: "<strong>Zero Liability for Modified / External Builds:</strong> We (the publisher and maintainer) assume <strong>no responsibility or liability whatsoever</strong> for any modified packages, third-party forks, repackaged binaries, unofficial distribution channels, or altered projects not originating directly from our official repositories. Any installation or use of modified, tampered, or third-party builds is entirely at your own risk, and the publisher assumes no responsibility for any consequences, damages, security compromises, or data breaches that may occur.",
                privSec1Title: "1. Executive Summary & Universal Ecosystem Overview",
                privSec1Body: "Our entire software portfolio—encompassing mobile apps, desktop programs, media engines, AI orchestrators, system utilities, security frameworks, command-line tools, and browser extensions across Android, Linux, Windows, and Web—is engineered from the ground up to prioritize user privacy, absolute data sovereignty, and uncompromised performance.",
                privSec1Commitment: "<strong>Core Privacy Commitment:</strong> All our tools, programs, and applications operate <strong>100% locally on your device</strong>. We do not collect, store, transmit, share, profile, or monetize any personal data, device identifiers, system logs, hardware streams, files, or user inputs to external analytics servers or third parties.",
                privSec2Title: "2. Information Processed On-Device",
                privSec2Intro: "To deliver core functionality, our software reads and processes the following information strictly on your local machine:",
                privSec2Item1: "<strong>Hardware & Media Streams:</strong> Any live device input (such as camera feed, audio stream, or GPU frame buffer) is processed strictly in real-time in volatile memory (RAM) and immediately discarded. Streams are never saved, recorded, or transmitted without explicit user command.",
                privSec2Item2: "<strong>User Inputs, Queries & Files:</strong> Text strings, files, commands, AI prompts, or URLs provided by the user are computed locally or routed strictly to endpoints configured by the user, without any central telemetry or logging.",
                privSec2Item3: "<strong>Local Storage & Preferences:</strong> User settings, history logs, caches, and customized parameters are stored strictly locally on your machine or device storage.",
                privSec3Title: "3. System Permissions & Privileges",
                privSec3Intro: "Our software only requests operating system privileges strictly required to carry out the specific features requested by the user:",
                privSec3Card1Title: "Hardware & Device Access",
                privSec3Card1Desc: "Used strictly in real-time when actively triggered by the user for media playback, capture, or processing. Never accessed or recorded silently in the background.",
                privSec3Card2Title: "Network & Connectivity",
                privSec3Card2Desc: "Utilized solely for user-initiated network requests (such as downloading files, resolving endpoints, or checking official updates on GitHub) with zero telemetry sent.",
                privSec3Card3Title: "File System & Storage",
                privSec3Card3Desc: "Used strictly to read or write files explicitly chosen by the user, manage application cache, and save exported data. No unauthorized disk indexing takes place.",
                privSec3Card4Title: "System Notifications & Status",
                privSec3Card4Desc: "Displays user-visible progress indicators, task completions, and essential operational status alerts on supported operating systems.",
                privSec4Title: "4. Safe Network & Resource Inspection",
                privSec4Body: "Whenever our utilities inspect or interact with network resources, they inspect only direct protocol responses to fulfill the user's task. Our software never reads, intercepts, or extracts private cookies, authentication credentials, or browsing history.",
                privSec5Title: "5. Zero Ads & No Tracking",
                privSec5Body: "Zero third-party analytics SDKs, zero telemetry collectors, and zero ads. We do not participate in behavioral tracking, device fingerprinting, or user profiling across any of our software solutions.",
                privSec6Title: "6. Data Retention & Deletion",
                privSec6Body: "All transient memory buffers are cleared instantly from RAM. Uninstalling any application or deleting its configuration folder permanently and completely purges all local history and preferences.",
                privSec7Title: "7. Managing Permissions & User Sovereignty",
                privSec7Body: "You maintain full control over all operating system permissions and tool execution. You can modify or revoke permissions at any time through your operating system settings.",
                privSec8Title: "8. Contact & Developer Support",
                privSec8Body: "If you have questions or feedback regarding this Privacy Policy across any of our software products, feel free to reach out directly.",
